# Deploy evidence is hashed BYTE-FOR-BYTE by assert_clean_checkout.py and
# record_provenance.py --verify, and CI runs on Linux while this workspace is
# Windows with core.autocrlf=true.
#
# Pass19: the first real GitHub Actions run failed at the readiness probe with
#   "artifact robotd_toml: sha256 differs from bundle"
# because the bundle recorded the WINDOWS WORKING-TREE bytes (CRLF, 9520 B,
# f6ebad3c...) while git stored / CI checked out the LF blob (9382 B,
# 2b054f78...). Three .onnx artifacts were byte-identical on both sides
# because git never text-converts binaries.
#
# Fix the root cause: pin this evidence file to LF in EVERY checkout, and keep
# the bundle fingerprints anchored to the committed blob bytes. A regression
# test (test_bundle_artifact_hashes_match_committed_blobs) checks that
# invariant using `git show HEAD:<path>` so no platform can drift silently.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
microduck-software/out/robotd_hd1910_mode0.toml text eol=lf

# Never let a future text-conversion rule touch the deployed policy graphs.
*.onnx binary
